  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "An idea I had was to possibly have some sort of hybrid system where some calculations would be done locally and some over network. Perhaps have a setting where you can select specific people to calculate local IK and everyone else network?\n\nExample: you have a somewhat decent PC and your playing on a public instance with some friends and other random people. let's say your friend just got full body and wanted to show it off, however network IK makes it seem laggy and unnatural. So, you click on your friend and enable the local IK option and boom, now only they are calculated locally and everyone else remains networked.\n\nGoing further, perhaps a way for the system to automatically split the calculations between your PC and the network, sort of like a YouTube video. The quality of tracking will increase or decrease based on users performance and network speed.",
